1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:16,010
All 50 questions from topics 11–15 with model answers – exactly as the examiner asks. Plus the 12 most important phrases and 5 mistakes that cost points. Get ready and answer out loud!

2
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:28,682
How does the task work? The examiner chooses two topics and asks four questions on each. That is eight questions in total, and each good answer gets one point.

3
00:00:29,567 --> 00:00:41,335
You know the topics in advance, but not the questions. So now we will go through all ten questions of each topic. Answer with a full sentence, ideally two, and listen to the tense.

4
00:00:42,233 --> 00:00:46,706
Topic 11: Free time and hobbies. Ten questions.

5
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,890
What do you do in your free time?

6
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:59,815
In my free time I read books, cook and go for walks.

7
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:07,251
Is this helping? Subscribe – there is a new video every day. And now the next question.

8
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:09,063
Do you have a hobby?

9
00:01:16,367 --> 00:01:20,597
Yes, my hobby is fishing. I go to the river with a friend.

10
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:23,284
How much free time do you have?

11
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,741
I have free time mainly in the evenings and on Sundays.

12
00:01:33,833 --> 00:01:36,153
Do you play a musical instrument?

13
00:01:43,467 --> 00:01:46,832
No, I don't, but I like listening to music.

14
00:01:47,933 --> 00:01:49,480
What music do you listen to?

15
00:01:56,767 --> 00:01:59,548
I mostly listen to pop and Ukrainian songs.

16
00:02:00,633 --> 00:02:03,140
What did you do in your free time as a child?

17
00:02:10,433 --> 00:02:13,768
As a child I played football and went to a dance club.

18
00:02:14,867 --> 00:02:17,600
What did you do in your free time last week?

19
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:27,749
Last week I went to the cinema and saw a new film.

20
00:02:28,833 --> 00:02:30,514
Do you have a new hobby?

21
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:41,040
Yes, I've started photographing nature with my phone.

22
00:02:42,133 --> 00:02:43,896
What will you do this evening?

23
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:53,739
This evening I'll read a book and listen to music.

24
00:02:54,833 --> 00:02:57,474
What hobby would you like to try?

25
00:03:04,767 --> 00:03:08,259
I'd like to try yoga because it's good for my back.

26
00:03:09,367 --> 00:03:13,018
Topic 12: Sport. Ten questions.

27
00:03:13,533 --> 00:03:14,702
Do you do any sport?

28
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,394
Yes, I do sport twice a week, I go running and swimming.

29
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:29,164
What's your favourite sport?

30
00:03:36,467 --> 00:03:39,251
I like football best, I play it with my son too.

31
00:03:40,367 --> 00:03:41,605
Where do you do sport?

32
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:51,299
I run in the park and swim in the town pool.

33
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:54,367
Do you watch sport on TV?

34
00:04:01,667 --> 00:04:04,329
Yes, I watch football, and ice hockey in winter.

35
00:04:05,433 --> 00:04:07,775
What sport is popular in your country?

36
00:04:15,067 --> 00:04:17,746
In my country football and boxing are the most popular.

37
00:04:18,833 --> 00:04:20,803
What sport did you do at school?

38
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:30,700
At school I played volleyball and ran.

39
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:33,460
When did you last do sport?

40
00:04:40,767 --> 00:04:44,458
Yesterday, I swam for half an hour.

41
00:04:45,567 --> 00:04:47,065
Why is sport important?

42
00:04:54,367 --> 00:04:57,991
Sport is important because it keeps us healthy and in a good mood.

43
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:00,727
Will you do sport at the weekend?

44
00:05:08,033 --> 00:05:10,550
Yes, on Saturday I'll play football with colleagues.

45
00:05:11,633 --> 00:05:13,584
What sport would you like to try?

46
00:05:20,900 --> 00:05:23,916
I'd like to try tennis because it looks fun.

47
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,605
Topic 13: Food and cooking. Ten questions.

48
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:30,151
What do you like to eat?

49
00:05:37,467 --> 00:05:40,278
I like pasta, chicken and vegetables.

50
00:05:41,367 --> 00:05:42,832
Who cooks at your home?

51
00:05:50,133 --> 00:05:53,114
Mostly I cook at home; at the weekend my wife cooks.

52
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:55,819
What do you usually cook?

53
00:06:03,133 --> 00:06:06,434
I usually cook soup, meat with potatoes or rice.

54
00:06:07,533 --> 00:06:09,006
What food don't you like?

55
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:18,722
I don't like fish because I don't like the taste.

56
00:06:19,833 --> 00:06:21,325
Where do you buy food?

57
00:06:28,633 --> 00:06:31,414
I buy food at the supermarket and vegetables at the market.

58
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:33,970
What Czech dish do you know?

59
00:06:41,267 --> 00:06:45,731
I know svíčková, goulash and dumplings. I like svíčková.

60
00:06:46,833 --> 00:06:49,395
What is a typical dish in your country?

61
00:06:56,700 --> 00:07:00,194
In my country borscht is typical; it's a beetroot soup.

62
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:02,619
What did you cook yesterday?

63
00:07:09,933 --> 00:07:12,271
Yesterday I cooked chicken with rice and a salad.

64
00:07:13,367 --> 00:07:14,742
What will you cook at the weekend?

65
00:07:22,033 --> 00:07:24,788
At the weekend I'll cook goulash because guests are coming.

66
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:28,260
What dish would you like to learn to cook?

67
00:07:35,567 --> 00:07:37,959
I'd like to learn to make Czech dumplings.

68
00:07:39,067 --> 00:07:43,360
Topic 14: Restaurant and café. Ten questions.

69
00:07:43,867 --> 00:07:45,262
Do you go to restaurants?

70
00:07:52,567 --> 00:07:54,875
I go to a restaurant about once a month.

71
00:07:55,967 --> 00:07:57,731
Who do you go to restaurants with?

72
00:08:05,033 --> 00:08:08,563
I go with my family or with colleagues from work.

73
00:08:09,667 --> 00:08:11,940
What do you usually order in a restaurant?

74
00:08:19,233 --> 00:08:22,597
I usually order soup and a main course, for example schnitzel.

75
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:24,978
What do you drink in a café?

76
00:08:32,267 --> 00:08:34,334
In a café I drink cappuccino or tea.

77
00:08:35,433 --> 00:08:37,236
How much is lunch in a restaurant?

78
00:08:44,533 --> 00:08:47,754
The lunch menu costs about one hundred fifty to two hundred crowns.

79
00:08:48,867 --> 00:08:50,917
Do you tip in restaurants?

80
00:08:58,233 --> 00:09:00,592
Yes, I usually give a ten percent tip.

81
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:03,798
When were you last in a restaurant?

82
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:14,256
I was last in a restaurant last Saturday at a birthday party.

83
00:09:15,367 --> 00:09:16,572
What did you eat there?

84
00:09:23,867 --> 00:09:26,186
I had pizza and drank lemonade.

85
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:29,056
Where will you go for dinner next time?

86
00:09:36,367 --> 00:09:39,450
Next time we'll go to the new Italian restaurant on the square.

87
00:09:40,533 --> 00:09:43,207
Which restaurant would you recommend to a friend?

88
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:54,148
I'd recommend a small restaurant by the river because they cook well there.

89
00:09:55,233 --> 00:09:59,077
Topic 15: Shopping. Ten questions.

90
00:09:59,567 --> 00:10:01,039
Where do you shop?

91
00:10:08,333 --> 00:10:10,537
I shop at a supermarket near my home.

92
00:10:11,633 --> 00:10:13,085
How often do you shop?

93
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:23,055
I do a big shop once a week, on Saturday.

94
00:10:24,167 --> 00:10:25,527
What do you buy most often?

95
00:10:32,833 --> 00:10:36,678
Most often I buy bread, milk, fruit and vegetables.

96
00:10:37,767 --> 00:10:39,386
Do you pay by card or cash?

97
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:49,433
Mostly I pay by card, it's faster.

98
00:10:50,533 --> 00:10:52,011
Do you shop online?

99
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:02,726
Yes, I buy clothes and electronics online.

100
00:11:03,833 --> 00:11:05,524
Who does the shopping in your home?

101
00:11:12,833 --> 00:11:15,814
My wife and I shop together, I carry the bags.

102
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:18,576
What did you buy last?

103
00:11:25,867 --> 00:11:28,094
Last I bought new winter boots.

104
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:30,729
How much did you pay for them?

105
00:11:38,033 --> 00:11:42,017
I paid one thousand two hundred crowns, they were on sale.

106
00:11:43,133 --> 00:11:44,990
What will you buy this week?

107
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:54,734
This week I'll buy a present for my daughter.

108
00:11:55,833 --> 00:11:58,417
What would you buy if you had a lot of money?

109
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:08,147
I would buy a new car and a big flat.

110
00:12:09,233 --> 00:12:13,940
Now the twelve most important phrases. Listen and repeat out loud.

111
00:12:14,633 --> 00:12:16,487
My name is Oleh Kovalenko.

112
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:22,000
I am from Ukraine, from Kharkiv.

113
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:27,233
I live in Kralupy nad Vltavou.

114
00:12:30,433 --> 00:12:31,933
I have been in Czechia for five years.

115
00:12:35,133 --> 00:12:36,333
I work in a warehouse.

116
00:12:39,533 --> 00:12:41,328
I have a wife and two sons.

117
00:12:44,533 --> 00:12:46,865
In my free time I like going for walks.

118
00:12:50,067 --> 00:12:52,629
I like the flat because it is bright.

119
00:12:55,833 --> 00:12:57,767
Last Saturday I was at the market.

120
00:13:00,967 --> 00:13:02,733
Next summer we will go to the sea.

121
00:13:05,933 --> 00:13:08,200
In five years I would like to have a better job.

122
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:13,600
I think I am calm and friendly.

123
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:19,858
Five typical mistakes that cost people points.

124
00:13:23,067 --> 00:13:29,292
Correct: Bydlím v Kralupech nad Vltavou. Answer with a full sentence, not one word.

125
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:38,609
Correct: Jsem z Ukrajiny. After the preposition z we use the 2nd case: z Ukrajiny, z Kyjeva.

126
00:13:42,300 --> 00:13:49,234
Correct: Bydlím v Praze. After the preposition v we use the 6th case: v Praze, v Brně.

127
00:13:52,933 --> 00:13:58,964
Correct: Je mi čtyřicet let. This is how we say age: je mi … let.

128
00:14:02,667 --> 00:14:10,419
Correct: Rodiče jsem naposledy viděl loni v létě. The question is in the past tense, so the answer must be too.

129
00:14:11,633 --> 00:14:33,329
Summary. First: answer with a full sentence, ideally two. Second: listen to the tense of the question and answer in the same tense. Third: watch the cases — z Ukrajiny, v Praze. And fourth: be specific — numbers, places, names.

130
00:14:34,533 --> 00:14:43,778
